<title>USA: EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 27-MAY					     .</title>
<headline>EMERGENCY WEATHER CONDITIONS -  WSC - 27-MAY					     .</headline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Depression 05W caused heavy rains and severe flooding over Luzon, Philippines on Monday. This system has moved east of Luzon and into the Philippine Sea where it is expected to intensify slowly while turning more northward, threatening some shipping. Conditions will continue to improve over Luzon over the next 12 hours.  </p>
<p>Tropical Depression 06W has formed near 10.1n/159.4e with top winds of near 30 mph. Slow intensification is forecast over the next 72 hours. This system will primarily threaten shipping.  </p>
<p>THERE ARE NO FURTHER EMERGENCY WEATHER STATEMENTS</p>
</text>
